From: Security Patch <security@apache.org>
Date: Mon, 1 Jan 2024 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Reject empty JSON property names for security

This patch addresses a vulnerability where empty JSON property names
can be used to bypass security settings. The empty key "" in JSON
payloads can inject arbitrary configuration values that override
security controls like the JavaScript enabled flag.

The fix adds a DruidSecurityModule that registers a DeserializationProblemHandler
to intercept and reject empty property names during JSON deserialization.

